3. To create derivatives for your personal use;
4. To copy and distribute unmodified copies of the Software for non-commercial purposes, provided that the full text of this License and the copyright notice are included.

"Personal use" means a single natural person using the Software for their own non-commercial purposes such as learning, research or personal creation, where the results are used by them or shared in a non-monetized personal space, and are not part of any organization, team or commercial activity.

Even as an individual user, any commercial use of the Software or its output is not covered by the free personal license in Section 1 (see Section 2).

## 2. Team use and commercial scenarios require a commercial license

Any of the following is not covered by the free personal license in Section 1 and requires prior contact with us to obtain a commercial license:

- **Team use**: any use by an organization (company, studio, institution, school, government body, etc.); or content production carried out under a team or studio name;
- **Commercial scenarios**: using the Software or its output for any commercial purpose, including but not limited to:
  - Commercial content production: commercial commissions, advertising and marketing, e-commerce content, paid courses, paid subscription content, or any distribution intended for profit;
  - Embedding or integrating the Software or its components into a commercial product, service or workflow;
  - Providing the Software to third parties as part of a service (SaaS, managed operations, outsourced production, etc.);
  - Reselling, leasing or paid distribution of the Software or its derivatives.

The form (individual / team / enterprise, per-seat or per-project) and pricing of the commercial license shall be set out in a commercial license agreement between the parties.

Contact: license@recut.video | https://recut.video

